<section class="saltydog-support">
  <h1>Salty Dog Mobile – FAQ &amp; Support</h1>

  <h2>General</h2>
  <p><strong>Q: What is Salty Dog Mobile?</strong><br>
  A: Salty Dog Mobile is an app for anglers and boaters to log catches, track trips, and view real-time weather and tide data.</p>
  <p><strong>Q: Is my data private?</strong><br>
  A: Yes. All your logs and data are stored locally on your device and are not shared unless you choose to export them.</p>

  <hr>

  <h2>Logging &amp; Tracking</h2>
  <p><strong>Q: How do I log a catch?</strong><br>
  A: Tap the “Mark Fishing Spot” button, fill in the details, and save your catch. You can add photos, notes, and location info.</p>
  <p><strong>Q: Can I edit or delete a log?</strong><br>
  A: Yes. Tap on any log entry to view, edit, or delete it.</p>
  <p><strong>Q: How do I view my fishing statistics?</strong><br>
  A: Tap the chart icon in the top right to see your stats and patterns.</p>

  <hr>

  <h2>Weather, Tides &amp; Marine Data</h2>
  <p><strong>Q: Where does the weather and tide data come from?</strong><br>
  A: The app uses Apple WeatherKit and NOAA for US marine data. International fallback is available via StormGlass (if enabled).</p>
  <p><strong>Q: Why don’t I see water temperature or tide info?</strong><br>
  A: These features require location access and internet connectivity. Some regions may not have available data.</p>
  <p><strong>Q: How often is the data updated?</strong><br>
  A: Weather and marine data refresh automatically as your location changes, or you can manually refresh by reopening the app.</p>

  <hr>

  <h2>Permissions &amp; Privacy</h2>
  <p><strong>Q: Why does the app need my location?</strong><br>
  A: Location is used to log catches, track your route, and fetch local weather/tide data. You can disable location, but some features won’t work.</p>
  <p><strong>Q: Does the app track me in the background?</strong><br>
  A: Only if you enable background location in settings. This helps track your route while fishing or boating.</p>

  <hr>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
  <p><strong>Q: Weather or tide data isn’t loading. What should I do?</strong><br>
    <ul>
      <li>Ensure you have an active internet connection.</li>
      <li>Make sure location permissions are enabled in your device settings.</li>
      <li>Try closing and reopening the app.</li>
      <li>If the issue persists, check for app updates in the App Store.</li>
    </ul>
  </p>
  <p><strong>Q: My catches or logs are missing.</strong><br>
    <ul>
      <li>Check if you’re logged into the correct device/user.</li>
      <li>Data is stored locally; if you deleted the app, logs may be lost unless exported.</li>
    </ul>
  </p>
  <p><strong>Q: The app is crashing or freezing.</strong><br>
    <ul>
      <li>Restart your device.</li>
      <li>Ensure you’re running the latest version of iOS and the app.</li>
      <li>If problems continue, contact support with details about your device and what you were doing when the issue occurred.</li>
    </ul>
  </p>

  <hr>

  <h2>Contact &amp; Support</h2>
  <p>If you need more help, contact us at <a href="mailto:support@saltydogapp.com">support@saltydogapp.com</a> or visit our website for updates and tips.</p>

